 style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Chelsea</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;this summer.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span>&#9632; </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;remain in talks with the architecture firm Populous over an Emirates Stadium expansion, with reports through the spring suggesting a capacity in the region of 80,000 and a &quot;shared reality&quot; technology component. Nothing has been formally lodged; treat capacity figures as speculative.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span>&#9632; The Champions League league-phase draw takes place in Nyon on Thursday, August 27 at 5pm BST. Six English clubs are in the pot: </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>, </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Liverpool</span><span>, </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Manchester City</span><span>, </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Chelsea</span><span>, </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Manchester United</span><span>&nbsp;and </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Aston Villa</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">. The final is at the Estadio Metropolitano in Madrid on June 5, 2027.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span>&#9632; </span><spa